IN THE SUPREME COURT OF INDIA
CASE NO: Criminal Appeal No. 1322 of 2021
CITATION: (2023) 8 SCC 632
YEAR: 2023

CORAM / BENCH:
Hon'ble Judges: S. Ravindra Bhat, Aravind Kumar

PARTIES:
Md. Asfak Alam vs State of Jharkhand

STATUTES & ACTS REFERRED:
Code of Criminal Procedure, 1973, Indian Penal Code, 1860

KEY PROVISIONS & SECTIONS:
Section 41 CrPC, Section 41A CrPC, Section 498A IPC

LEGAL KEYWORDS & TOPICS:
arnesh kumar compliance, mechanical remand, police notices

================================================================================
                    JUDGMENT SUMMARY & RATIO DECIDENDI
================================================================================

Strictly directed courts and police forces nationwide to enforce Arnesh Kumar guidelines and penalize officers engaging in unlawful or mechanical arrests.

1. ISSUES CONSIDERED:
   The court addressed questions of legal interpretation under Section 41 CrPC, Section 41A CrPC, Section 498A IPC.

2. ANALYSIS & PRECEDENT CONTEXT:
   Having examined the statutory scheme, fundamental principles of jurisprudence,
   and constitutional safeguards, the Court reiterated the necessity of strict
   compliance with statutory procedure and evidentiary standards.

3. HELD & BINDING RATIO:
   The principle formulated in this judgment constitutes binding judicial precedent
   within its territorial and appellate jurisdiction.

